# 6. AUTHENTICATION ARCHITECTURE

Authentication flow:

React Native
↓
Login API
↓
Email + Password
↓
Backend
↓
User lookup
↓
bcrypt password verification
↓
JWT generation
↓
Access Token
↓
React Native token storage
↓
Authenticated API requests

Protected requests use:

Authorization: Bearer <token>

Backend middleware:

authenticateToken

Responsibilities:

* Extract Bearer token
* Verify JWT
* Decode userId
* Decode role
* Attach authenticated user to request
* Reject invalid/expired tokens

---

# 7. RBAC ARCHITECTURE

RBAC means:

Role → Access

Roles:

Super Admin
Principal
Teacher
Student

Authorization middleware:

requireRole(...roles)

Example:

Principal-only API
↓
authenticateToken
↓
requireRole('principal')
↓
Controller

Unauthorized role:

HTTP 403

Unauthenticated request:

HTTP 401

